   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 405 of the laws of 2007, amending the tax law relating to increasing hotel/motel taxes in Chautauqua county, in relation to extending the expiration of such provisions",
    "basePrintNo": "S4022",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4022-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 405 of 2007",
    "lawSection": "Chautauqua County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4022\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act\nto amend chapter\n405 of the laws of 2007, amending the tax law relating to\nincreasing hotel/motel taxes in Chautauqua county, in relation to\nextending the expiration of such provisions\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend to November 30,2013, the\nexpiration of the 5% hotel and motel tax in the County of Chautauqua.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 2 of chapter 405 of the Laws of 2007, amending the tax law, as\namended by chapter 130 of the laws of 2009, is amended.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Chautauqua County Legislature passed a resolution requesting the\nauthority to extend the county's authorization for an occupancy tax\nof up to five percent. Chapter 405 of the Laws of 2007\nauthorized Chautauqua County to raise their occupancy tax from three\nto five percent.\nChapter 130 of the Laws of 2009 subsequently authorized an extension\nuntil November 30, 2011. This bill would provide an additional\ntwo-year extension until November 30, 2013.\n\nThe additional tax revenue will be placed in a fund dedicated to the\nenhancement and protection of the lakes and streams of Chautauqua\nCounty. The beautiful lakes and streams located in Chautauqua County\nare a primary attraction for tourists and visitors.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
